(Plan 281: a function call inside an explicit {...} group must use its own)
(of/to connectors even when nested inside a construct that reserves that)
(connector for itself - here, byte's own "of".)

To ci with a number called x and a number called y.
  Return a number, x add y.

To id with a number called x.
  Return a number, x.

a buffer called buf is 10 bytes in size.
Set byte 3 of buf to 42.
Print byte {ci of 1 and 2} of buf.

Set byte 3 of buf to 99.
Print byte {id of 3} of buf.
